# BUG-241 regression fixture.
#
# std.Progress.start gained an `Io` parameter in Zig 0.16; the preamble still called it
# with one argument, so EVERY program touching `Progress.` failed to build. It went unseen
# for months because test/progress_test.zbr carried no registration, and a file that has
# never passed cannot regress a baseline.
#
# There is nothing to assert about a progress bar's rendering here on purpose:
# std.Progress detects a non-tty and draws nothing under a gate runner. Compiling and
# running to completion IS the regression check.
def main()
    var pb = Progress.bar(3, "work")
    for n in 0:3
        pb.tick()
    pb.done()
    print("bug241: OK")
